    <div class="about-label">| Who We Are</div>

    <h2>KSK Foundation: Empowering Young People for a Better Future</h2>

    <p class="herop">
      KSK Foundation is a registered Non-Governmental Organization headquartered
      at Plot 24A Hannington Road, Kampala, Uganda. Since its founding in 2011,
      the Foundation has championed Leadership, Innovation and Enterprise as
      pillars for community empowerment and poverty eradication.
    </p>

    <div class="about-details">
      <h3>Our Mission</h3>
      <p class="herop">
        To equip young people with practical, real-world skills in leadership,
        innovation and enterprise — turning potential into competitive,
        career-ready talent.
      </p>

      <h3>Our Approach</h3>
      <p class="herop">
        Each KSK Foundation program pairs structured curriculum with mentorship
        from working professionals. Cohorts are intentionally kept small and
        selective, with participants shortlisted through structured interviews
        and scored assessments so facilitators can give real, individual
        attention.
      </p>

      <p class="herop">
        Programs culminate in a practical showcase — a Hackathon, a project
        pitch, or a graduation ceremony — where participants demonstrate what
        they've built, not just what they've learned.
      </p>
    </div>

